            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "This disclaimer isn't acceptable. Each change you propose is done so on the basis of your judgement, and you are responsible for it in its entirety: You cannot outsource this responsibility. If you don't yet understand the work, please take the time to do so before proposing it, at which point this disclaimer is unnecessary.\n\nIt is enough that you provide your `Signed-off-by:` tag. That says to me you stand behind it, and take responsibility for any of its failings.\n\nPlease remove this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Sure, removed it and re-wrote the thing as a shell script which gets rid of the nested Makefile templates and IMO overall simpler and easier to understand.\n\nAlso more in line with the existing `scripts/` which AFAIK do not make use of makefiles."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "I see `make` as a domain-specific scripting language. I don't feel it's necessary to constrain ourselves to one scripting language in `scripts/`.\n\n\nIn the future I ask that you discuss concerns and develop consensus before proposing patches that take a much different direction to what we have (this current patchset being an example, but not a particularly critical one).\n\nThe alternative was becoming comfortable with `make` as a language."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> I see make as a domain-specific scripting language. I don't feel it's necessary to constrain ourselves to one scripting language in scripts/.\n\nSure but we already have shell, awk, perl, C, C++, meson, ninja, ...\nat some point we have to stop. I am not saying this is the point but if we can achieve the same goal with a tool we are already using, it is simpler for folks to contribute without having to learn a new thing.\n\n> In the future I ask that you discuss concerns and develop consensus \nbefore proposing patches that take a much different direction to what we\n have\n\nSure, i will try to keep it in mind."
                },
                {
                    "file": "scripts/crater",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "This is a bit shouty and pretty verbose. Can we just call this `crater`?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "scripts/crater",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "re-wrote our crater as a shell script, IMO it is simpler that way."
                },
                {
                    "file": "scripts/crater",
                    "line": 43,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
